  "knowledgePattern": "Combine equal-bound integrals and cancel squared cross terms",
  "knowledgeTags": [
    "calculus"
  ],
  "solution": "<p>Linearity lets us subtract the integrands first, because both integrals have the same limits.</p><p>With <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math> throughout <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>The required difference is therefore <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mn>9</mn><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></msubsup><mn>4</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\" /><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>28</mn></mrow></math>. Answer F. No integration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> is needed.</p>",
  "hints": [
